arget code was not changed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"no-domain-drift\",\n      \"verdict\": \"upheld\",\n      \"evidence\": \"git diff main...HEAD --stat -- src/domain/ src/rulepack/ produced empty output.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"no-rulepack-territory\",\n      \"verdict\": \"upheld\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The required rule-term scan over every non-test .ts file in src/lib/import/stb produced NO_RULE_TERMS_NON_TEST_SOURCE. The source-only numeric review found only parser/application mechanics; scope-guard.test.ts still declares the complete forbidden term list.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"name-not-overwritten\",\n      \"verdict\": \"upheld\",\n      \"evidence\": \"apply.test.ts asserts result.project.name is unchanged and StbImport.test.tsx asserts the store project name is unchanged in the approval flows. The temporary project-name overwrite mutation broke 3 tests.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"refusal-preserves-project\",\n      \"verdict\": \"upheld\",\n      \"evidence\": \"apply.test.ts asserts changed-grid and changed-story refusals return applied:false and preserve the original project reference. Removing a refusal temporarily broke 2 tests.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"same-span-keeps-members\",\n      \"verdict\": \"upheld\",\n      \"evidence\": \"apply.test.ts contains the explicit 'keeps members when only labels change on an otherwise equal grid' case. Removing the same-span preservation branch temporarily broke that test.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"issues-survive-approval\",\n      \"verdict\": \"upheld\",\n      \"evidence\": \"StbImport.test.tsx passes the issue-bearing candidate through approval and asserts the issue remains visible. Temporarily clearing candidate.issues after approval broke 'keeps issues and unsupported elements visible after approval'.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"no-network-in-import\",\n      \"verdict\": \"refuted\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The required test-inclusive scan matched src/lib/import/stb/scope-guard.test.ts:49 ('fetch'), :50 ('XMLHttpRequest'), and :52 ('sendBeacon'). Runtime import sources contain no network call and telemetry contains no file-name or file-content payload handling.\",\n      \"note\": \"The matches are guard vocabulary strings, not runtime network calls, but the premise's stated scan includes tests and is not zero. Target code was not changed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"no-new-dependency\",\n      \"verdict\": \"upheld\",\n      \"evidence\": \"git diff main...HEAD --stat -- package.json package-lock.json produced empty output.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mismatch-issue-still-bites\",\n      \"verdict\": \"upheld\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The mismatch issue is asserted by src/lib/import/stb/candidates.test.ts:268 and tests/fixtures/stb-import/expected/diffchecker-filea.json, and candidates.ts:127 adds it. Temporarily suppressing that line caused 2 failing tests: the UI candidate mismatch test and the diffchecker-filea candidate fixture test. The line was restored.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ledgers-not-fabricated\",\n      \"verdict\": \"upheld\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The step-5 docs diff contains only docs/MILESTONES.md and docs/RISKS.md; ADR.md, PRD.md, ARCHITECTURE.md, and SOURCES.md are unchanged. Direct inventory found document=5, expected=5, applied=5, synthetic=2; STB_ISSUES=18 and STB_APPLY_REFUSALS=4; SOURCES.md records 4 real fixtures, RC real sample version 2.0.1, no realistic 2.1 corpus, and code-search total_count 9. These match the ledger values and the CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md ST-Bridge summary.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"applied-fixtures-are-oracles\",\n      \"verdict\": \"upheld\",\n      \"evidence\": \"All 5 applied fixtures exist and each _derivedFrom points to the same-named expected fixture. Independent expected-to-applied derivation matched: diffchecker-filea X=1000,2000,2000,4400,4400,1000; Y=1000,3200,3200,3200,3200,3200,3200,1000; heights=4500,4000,4000,3800; d